	(title_block
		(title "VMT 04/16 controller - Outputs")
		(date "2026-11-03")
		(rev "0.1")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "Outputs\nPotential-free relays, coils driven from the MCU (low-side driver). De-energised = off.\nContacts switch TE_L+ -> CMD_HEAT / CMD_COOL / CMD_COND_FAN, and T_L+ -> CMD_LIGHT (as 2S2 did).\nCOMP_1K10 = TE_L+ via diode (as 2V51) - see Signal_list V3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "164a802a-deb5-454f-bb90-be257551e66a")
	)
	(text_box "TO DESIGN\n- 4 potential-free contacts, replacing 3K2 / 3K1 / 2K17 / 2S2:\n  TE_L+ -> CMD_HEAT,  TE_L+ -> CMD_COOL,  TE_L+ -> CMD_COND_FAN,  T_L+ -> CMD_LIGHT.\n- Solid state, not mechanical: heating runs time-proportional (~2 s period), a relay contact would wear out within a few thousand operating hours.\n- Input LEDs driven straight from MCU GPIO via series resistor. 100k pull-down on each input: MCU reset or hang = all outputs off.\n- Loads are on PL1: relay coils 1K4 / 1K9 / 1K2 and heater SSR 1V6 (via F7). Measure currents (Signal_list V6). TVS across each output against coil kick-back.\n- COMP_1K10 = TE_L+ through a diode (as 2V51) - confirm Signal_list V3 first.\n- Optional: indicator LED per output for commissioning.\n\nCOMPONENT PROPOSAL\n- PhotoMOS relay, 60 V / >= 0.5 A, e.g. Panasonic AQY21x / AQV21x series (check voltage and load ratings against V6).\n- LED series resistor: ~270-470 Ohm at 3V3 (set for the PhotoMOS LED current in the datasheet).\n- TVS: SMBJ30A per output. COMP_1K10 diode: S1M (1 A / 1000 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 50.8 0)
